# 30-no-secrets allowlist: one line per allowlisted hit.
# Format: EXEMPT <repo-relative path> | <token> | <reason>
# <token> is the exact text `git grep -o` matched (the command is in the stage header).
# An entry exempts that token at that path only. The same token at another path, or any other
# value in the same file, is still RED. There are no path-wide or pattern-wide exemptions.
# Every field is required and a malformed line turns the stage RED. Listed 2026-09-24
# (jev-09qj) when the scan widened from foundation/ to every committable file; each hit was
# read in context before it was listed.
EXEMPT compaction/test/omp-binding.test.ts | TYPESAFE_API_KEY = 'test-key-never-sent | test placeholder: sets the variable so fromEnv registers a handler; the test asserts the asker makes no network call
EXEMPT demos/test/live-state.test.mjs | TYPESAFE_API_KEY: 'offline-placeholder | test placeholder for a child process whose fetch is replaced by a capturing preload; never sent
EXEMPT docs/demos/upstream-repro/compaction-install-run-20260919.md | TYPESAFE_API_KEY=deliberately-broken | recorded negative probe: the prose above it says a deliberately invalid key was used
EXEMPT work/.selftest-30-allow.tmp | TYPESAFE_API_KEY="selftest-placeholder-not-a-key | selftest fixture: exists only while --selftest runs, to prove an entry binds path and token together
